course: dictionary
lesson: 10109
title: Organising ideas: firstly, secondly, thirdly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When you give reasons or steps, the reader needs to know where each one starts. «Thirdly» is a signpost word: it tells the reader that this is your third point, after «firstly» and «secondly». «Firstly, wash your hands. Secondly, sit down. Thirdly, eat your lunch.» The steps are clear because each word shows the order.
explain: Writers and speakers use this pattern for persuasive writing and speeches. A good list often goes: «firstly, secondly, thirdly, finally». Each signpost helps the listener follow your thinking, so they do not get lost in your argument.
explain: In the old classic The Wind in the Willows, the charges against Toad are listed in order: «first, of stealing a valuable motor-car; secondly, of driving to the public danger; and, thirdly, of gross impertinence to the rural police.» Notice that the word «thirdly» sits in the middle of the sentence, after «and», and it still signals the third point. Impertinence means rude cheek.
fact: «Thirdly» is an adverb, and it means used to introduce the third point in a list of reasons or steps.
fact: «Thirdly» comes after «firstly» and «secondly».
fact: Signpost words such as «firstly, secondly, thirdly, finally» help organise ideas in writing and speeches.
fact: «Impertinence» means rude cheek.
fact: Use a signpost word at the start of a point so the reader knows its place in the list.
exercise: «First, of stealing a valuable motor-car; secondly, of driving to the public danger; and, thirdly, of gross impertinence to the rural police.» Which word introduces the third point? | secondly | firstly | *thirdly | and
exercise: Which word could start a list of three reasons, as the third point? | *Thirdly | Blue | Quickly | Secondly
exercise: Ben is writing a speech. He has given two reasons. Which word should he use for his third reason? | Firstly | *Thirdly | Before | Secondly
test: Complete the list: «Firstly, wash your hands. Secondly, sit down. ___, eat your lunch.» | *Thirdly | Sadly | Firstly | Secondly
test: Which word is the adverb that introduces the third point in a list? | Thirteen | Thirsty | Third | *Thirdly
exam: In the sentence about three offences, «gross impertinence» is a charge. What does impertinence mean? | *Rude cheek | A large hat | Strong wind | Sleepy yawn
